   "source": [
    "# Per-cohort substitution-type subtype analysis (see analyze_cohort):\n",
    "#   - Friedman test on SAAPs present in ALL disease states (complete blocks)\n",
    "#   - pairwise Wilcoxon (each disease vs CTRL) on partially-present SAAPs\n",
    "# Significant aa_sub log2(RAAS/CTRL) heatmaps for ACG, FC, and the pooled Brain cohort.\n",
    "grouped = prep_cohort(SAAP_quant_df_grouped)\n",
    "pooled = prep_cohort(SAAP_quant_df_pooled)\n",
    "analyze_cohort(grouped[grouped['Dataset'] == 'acg'].copy(), 'ACG')\n",
    "analyze_cohort(grouped[grouped['Dataset'] == 'fc'].copy(), 'FC')\n",
    "analyze_cohort(pooled[pooled['Dataset'] == 'brain'].copy(), 'Brain')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3782f817",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Statistical analysis of substitution-type RAAS trends — between tissues and with disease\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tissue effect (per AAS):** one-way ANOVA of Reporter_RAAS across tissues with Tukey HSD post-hoc, one test per substitution type (`run_anova_by_tissue`); F-statistics ranked and BH-FDR corrected. **Variance decomposition:** one-way ANOVA F of RAAS across the levels of each factor (substitution type, disease, tissue) to compare how much RAAS variance each explains. **Tissue × disease (per AAS):** log2FC vs tissue-specific CTRL plus a one-way ANOVA of RAAS across disease groups within each (tissue, AAS), run at both SAAP- and replicate-level aggregation, BH-FDR corrected. P/q/F values are reported in scientific notation."
   ]
  },
